  "featured_image_url": "https://thedrakelawfirm.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Colorado-Lawyer-Marie-Drake-Says-Passage-of-New-Law-a-Victory-for-Parents.jpg",
  "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>GOLDEN, Colorado – <a href=\"https://thedrakelawfirm.com/about-the-firm/\">Marie Drake</a>, Attorney and CEO of The Drake Law Firm, P.C., applauds the recent passage of Colorado’s “Affirm Parentage Adoption in Assisted Reproduction” Bill <a href=\"https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/hb22-1153\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HB22-1153</a>. The bill was signed into law by Governor Jared Polis on May 23, 2022, and was co-sponsored by Senator Jeff Bridges, Majority Leaders Dominick Moreno and Daneya Esgar, and Representative Kerry Tipper.</p>\n<p>The bill, also known as &#8220;Marlo&#8217;s Law,&#8221; was named in honor of Marlo, the daughter of Heather Palm and her wife Majority Leader Esgar who was also co-sponsor of the bill.</p>\n<p>Marlo&#8217;s Law updated Colorado&#8217;s outdated parentage law and went into effect on August 10, 2022. The law ensures that all parents who conceive through assisted reproductive technology (ART) are entitled to the same rights and legal protections regardless of their marital status, sexual orientation, or gender identity. It also affirms parentage by adoption for a person who did not give birth when the child&#8217;s conception resulted from ART.</p>\n<p>Since the advent of ART, Colorado law had not been updated in a significant way, making it difficult for ART-formed families to obtain assured, nationwide legal recognition without being subjected to discrimination.</p>\n<p>“As a family and <a href=\"https://thedrakelawfirm.com/family-law/adoption/\">adoption lawyer</a>, this is a victory in removing obstacles to becoming a legally recognized parent if a child has been conceived via ART. The bill’s passage also highlights Colorado’s commitment to supporting equality for all parents,” says Drake.</p>\n<h2>About The Drake Law Firm</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://thedrakelawfirm.com/\">The Drake Law Firm, P.C.</a> is a full-service law firm with offices in Golden and Colorado, focusing primarily on family law, divorce, child custody, and child support. The Drake Law Firm also offers real estate and business law services. Founded in 2011, it has provided countless clients in Colorado and the entire Rocky Mountains region with solution-oriented legal representation for over a decade. The Drake Law Firm prides itself on taking a proactive approach to its clients’ cases and has made it a part of its core mission to give undivided, individualized attention to every client according to their needs. Take advantage of a free, 15-minute consultation by calling <a href=\"tel:303-261-8111\">(303) 261-8111</a> or filling out the online <a href=\"https://thedrakelawfirm.com/contact-us/\">contact form</a>.</p>\n"
  },
